│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ stress_gated_diversification                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Shift from nearly always choosing structural mutation to a stress-gated heredity policy.  │
│                          │ Structural edits remain favored when diversity is low and the population is not           │
│                          │ collapsing, but mixed mutation takes over under real demographic stress, parametric       │
│                          │ mutation is favored for productive parents, and cloning gets a narrow role for stable     │
│                          │ high-energy lineages. This should preserve the current birth-rate advantage from          │
