│ patch_name               │ crisis_mixed_refine_balance                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This edit keeps the current successful parametric/structural balance but makes the policy │
│                          │ more state-conditional. It adds a compact refinement signal for productive, complex       │
│                          │ parents, a novelty signal for simple genomes when diversity is low, and a crisis signal   │
│                          │ for post-event declines. Parametric is slightly favored for productive complex lineages,  │
│                          │ structural is focused on low-complexity novelty opportunities, and mixed receives a gated │
│                          │ boost only during population decline plus stress/scarcity. This should preserve the high  │
│                          │ survival/birth profile while giving the evaluator a chance to use mixed mutations in the  │
│                          │ rare recovery states where combined structural and parametric change is likely more       │
│                          │ productive.                                                                               │
